# .claudeignore — files AI coding tools should not read, index, or hand-edit.
#
# ENFORCEMENT: Claude Code does not natively read .claudeignore. In this repo a
# PreToolUse hook (.claude/hooks/claudeignore_guard.py, wired in
# .claude/settings.local.json) reads THIS file and denies any Read/Grep/Glob
# whose target matches a pattern below. Patterns are gitignore-style; `!`
# negates; last match wins. Other tools that read .claudeignore (Cursor, the
# li-zhixin/claude-ignore hook, etc.) also honor it.
#
# Note: hook registration lives in settings.local.json (gitignored / per-dev),
# so move that hooks block to .claude/settings.json to enforce team-wide.

# ── Secrets — never read (live DB / Graph / Octopus / Bexio creds) ──
*.env
!env/*.env.example
env.json
ngrok.yaml

# ── Python bytecode & caches ──
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class

# ── Virtualenvs / vendored dependencies ──
.venv/
venv/
node_modules/

# ── Build & packaging artifacts ──
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
*.egg
htmlcov/
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml

# ── Tool caches / type-checker & linter indexes ──
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/

# ── Code-intelligence & agent index / state files ──
.gitnexus/
ruvector.db
.swarm/
.claude-flow/
.superpowers/
!.superpowers/sdd/
.playwright-mcp/
.claude/memory.db
.claude/cache/
.claude/logs/

# ── Lock files (machine-generated, large, noisy) ──
uv.lock

# ── Generated code — auto-dumped from the INT DB; never hand-edit ──
# Left READABLE on purpose (commented = documented but NOT enforced): CLAUDE.md
# uses these per-object DDL dumps + the .pot template for schema / i18n search.
# Regenerated by sql/sync-from-db.py and pybabel; go through a migration/extract.
#   sql/NexoraDB/
#   sql/GeneraliDB/
#   messages.pot
# Compiled message catalogs are binary — safe to skip entirely.
translations/*/LC_MESSAGES/*.mo

# ── Runtime data (logs, sessions, screenshots, public uploads) ──
var/
static/uploads/
/logs/
